          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression is a direct, present-tense avowal of the speaker's love for Maria. Its placement in the asseverative construction “Saavist … saavist” presents that emotional state emphatically as true in response to her doubts.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The focal words themselves report love rather than undertake an action, obligation, or defined relationship. The longer turn separately introduces enduring companionship—living and dying with Maria—but that neighbouring undertaking should not be transferred onto the marked avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The focal expression is a deliberate answer to Maria's request for reassurance and is framed as a reasoned, solemn assertion. The evidence does not present it as a reflex-like affective discharge, notwithstanding the emotionally intense reunion.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"reason\":\"The focal expression's core force is adequately captured as an emphatic avowal of love. No additional core function distinct from truth-presenting, commitment, or expressive discharge is supported.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"During an emotional reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent change is genuine and lasting rather than a temporary reaction to longing. He answers her directly and solemnly with the focal avowal.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The marked expression itself contains no undertaking. In the surrounding turn, the narrator does present a future-oriented relational commitment by saying that Maria is the person with whom he will live a very long time and die. Maria's tears and happiness show that she accepts his speech as truthful reassurance, although the supplied passage does not formalise the terms of any undertaking or explicitly record a separate verbal acceptance.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work from the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly represents the avowal as sincere through the narrator's prior self-reflection and Maria's narrated understanding, but this remains literary representation. The supplied scene does not establish later fulfilment of the surrounding future-oriented commitment.\"}"
        }
